pr_body:
Fixes #114401
 
Allows a `semantic_text` field to be in an object field:

```json
PUT test_semantic

PUT /test_semantic/_mapping
{
  "properties": {
    "level_1": {
      "properties": {
        "level_2": {
          "type": "semantic_text",
          "inference_id": "elser-endpoint"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

POST test_semantic/_doc/0001
{
  "level_1": {
    "level_2": "text"
  }
}
```

issue_context.body:
### Elasticsearch Version

8.15.0 - 8.15.3

### Installed Plugins

_No response_

### Java Version

_bundled_

### OS Version

Darwin

### Problem Description

`semantic_text` fields are not currently supported in object fields. 

An object field that contains semantic_text will fail when a document is ingested that has content for the semantic_text field.

### Steps to Reproduce

The following steps:

```json
PUT test_semantic

PUT /test_semantic/_mapping
{
  "properties": {
    "level_1": {
      "properties": {
        "level_2": {
          "type": "semantic_text",
          "inference_id": "elser-endpoint"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

POST test_semantic/_doc/0001
{
  "level_1": {
    "level_2": "text"
  }
}
```

fails with:

```json
{
  "error": {
    "root_cause": [
      {
        "type": "document_parsing_exception",
        "reason": "[1:29] failed to parse field [level_1.level_2] of type [semantic_text] in document with id '0001'. Preview of field's value: 'null'"
      }
    ],
    "type": "document_parsing_exception",
    "reason": "[1:29] failed to parse field [level_1.level_2] of type [semantic_text] in document with id '0001'. Preview of field's value: 'null'",
    "caused_by": {
      "type": "illegal_argument_exception",
      "reason": "[1:29] [semantic_text] Expected START_OBJECT but was: END_OBJECT"
    }
  },
  "status": 400
}
```

